  "reason": "Revision 5 Adversarial revalidation found that TransitionCommit could bind a valid review_id to a valid next_state owned by a different review, allowing a contradictory cross-review transition intent to reach the backend-neutral persistence boundary. Revision 6 adds the minimal cross-field invariant requiring TransitionCommit.review_id to exactly equal TransitionCommit.next_state.review_id, with focused regression coverage. Because this correction tightens authoritative review/state binding, the review reopens at Adversarial and the full five-stage program remains required before implementation may continue beyond the skeleton.",
